  <bpmn:process id="L4_05_P_SPON_PROCESS" name="Sponsor" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation textFormat="text/plain">C-01 decisions 2-4 of 4: G3 'Serious breach?' (EU, REQ-105, REQ-111), G6 'Serious noncompliance?' (ICH, REQ-118, REQ-119); decision 4 (IRB serious or continuing noncompliance, REQ-124) stays inside the collapsed IRB/IEC pool and appears only as message flows M8 and M9.
C-05: start event S1 is the same event as the L4-04 start and starts the EU 7-day clock; whose awareness counts stays [verify] (REQ-111).
C-03: the binding US duty (REQ-121, [verify]) and the DRAFT split (REQ-122, REQ-123) are separate tasks A9 and A10, so A10 and its flow M7 show DRAFT; the model does not state that minor deviations are exempt.
Jurisdiction pattern: AND split G1 into an EU path (XOR 'EU CTR applies?') and the ICH path, so the EU serious breach decision and the ICH serious noncompliance decision never exclude each other.</bpmn:documentation>
